## 🧠 How It Works

The program first asks the user to enter:

* Name
* Weight in kilograms
* Height in meters

The BMI is calculated using the formula:

```text
BMI = Weight / (Height × Height)
```

In Python:

```python
bmi = weight / (height * height)
```

The `round()` function is then used to display the BMI up to two decimal places.

## 📊 BMI Categories

The program classifies the calculated BMI using these ranges:

|   BMI Range | Category     |
| ----------: | ------------ |
|  Below 18.5 | Underweight  |
| 18.5 – 24.9 | Normal range |
|   25 – 29.9 | Overweight   |
| 30 or above | Obesity      |

> **Note:** BMI is a general screening measure and does not by itself provide a complete assessment of health.

